Package: styloprofile
Type: Package
Title: Stylometric Reference Profiles and Outlier Distances
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Armand", "Surbakti", email = "actuallyarmand@gmail.com",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Extracts interpretable stylometric features from documents and
    measures how far a document sits from a reference distribution by two
    complementary routes: a Cholesky-based squared Mahalanobis distance, which
    responds to a document being extreme, and an angular distance derived from
    cosine similarity, which responds to the proportions between features being
    wrong. Reference corpora are assembled from OpenAlex, with the topic,
    journal and date window as arguments. Intended for studying whether machine-generated
    text is a statistical outlier relative to human writing, following the
    feature-based framing of Froehling and Zubiaga (2021)
    <doi:10.7717/peerj-cs.443>, the distance of Mahalanobis (1936), the vector
    space model of Salton, Wong and Yang (1975) <doi:10.1145/361219.361220>,
    and the metric angular form of van Dongen and Enright (2012)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.1208.3145>.
